hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19287","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Kathir, freedman of the Laythiyyin, informed us from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What is for me, O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the path of Allah? He said: Paradise. When he turned he said: Except debt; Jibril confided it to me just now, upon him be peace."
"19288","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Kathir, freedman of the Hilaliyyin, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh from his father who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is for me if I fight in the path of Allah until I am killed? He said: Paradise. When he turned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except debt; Jibril confided it to me, upon him be peace."
